Chunk: PAs can be depolymerized by a cutinase called Thc_Cut1, in which the promiscuous amidase activity was enhanced ( Biundo et al., 2019 ). Residues that may prevent water molecules from interacting with the transition state were chosen for mutation, resulting in a 6–15-fold increase in hydrolytic activity ( Biundo et al., 2019 ). In addition, bifunctional biocatalysts for increased depolymerization efficiency have been created by fusing a plastic-degrading enzyme with another supporting enzyme. For instance, based on the concept that lipase largely cleaves the polymeric backbone of PCL into low-molecular-weight oligomers, a fusion protein composed of lipase and cutinase (Lip-Cut) was developed with significantly increased PCL hydrolysis activity. In contrast, cutinase further hydrolyzes these low-molecular weight oligomers into soluble ones. Similarly, compared with wild-type PETase, a synergistic fusion of PETase and MHETase has been shown to triple the hydrolysis efficiency of PET.
