Chunk: large-scale reduction of environmental pollution and encouraging economic expansion.    7  Future directions  Emerging research underscores the need to standardize methodologies for isolating microorganisms that produce plastic-degrading enzymes. This will increase enzyme yields from pure colonies, which in turn will accelerate the polymer degradation process. Bio-upcycling is increasingly recognized as a viable solution to the problem of plastic waste. However, its commercialization has not yet fully materialized, despite ongoing efforts to identify microorganisms and enzymes capable of degrading and valorizing plastic waste. Further investigation into multi-enzyme or multi-microbial strategies is necessary to overcome these challenges; systems metabolic engineering is critical for creating strains of microbes with enhanced capabilities for degrading and monetizing plastic.
